  "patch": "Looking at the incident, the issue is clear: at line 136 in main.py, the code attempts to format `sku` as a decimal integer using `format(sku, \"03d\")`, but `sku` is a string parameter.\n\nThe previous candidate tried `format(int(sku), \"03d\")` but this still fails because the provoking request has `sku=WIDGET`, which is not numeric and cannot be converted to int.\n\nThe root cause is that the code assumes `sku` is numeric, but the API accepts any string as a SKU (as evidenced by the request `GET /quote?sku=WIDGET`). The fix is to use a string format code instead of a decimal format code.\n\n--- a/alpha/main.py\n+++ b/alpha/main.py\n@@ -133,7 +133,7 @@ def quote(sku: str, quantity: int = 1, code: str = \"\") -> dict:\n     return {\"sku\": sku, \"quantity\": quantity,\n             \"per_unit\": round(total / quantity, 2),\n             \"total\": round(total, 2),\n-            \"reference\": \"Q\" + format(sku, \"03d\")}\n+            \"reference\": \"Q\" + format(sku, \"s\")}\n \n \n @app.get(\"/orders/{order_id}/discounted\")",
